Make sure pulseaudio was compiled with bluetooth support, having these
two present at build time:

	bluez
	sbc

Or better just check the optional deps in:

	https://crux.nu/ports/crux-3.8/opt/pulseaudio/Pkgfile

This is needed, because the early load in /etc/pulse/default.pa at line
66 doesn't seem to work properly (probably because bluetooth isn't ready
yet at that point). Pulseaudio evidently accepts this second load.

If pulseaudio ever refuses to start after an update, this double load is
the first thing to suspect.
